juno-kde-fancontrol (0.4.0+diamon1) unstable; urgency=low

  * The GPU fan gets its own curve on dGPU machines. pwm1 keeps the CPU
    temperature, pwm2 now follows the dGPU: the editor gains an "Editing:
    CPU fan / GPU fan" selector with one curve per fan, and knob mode writes
    one `# Knobs pwmN:` line per fan with per-fan executable FCTEMPS sources
    (new /usr/bin/juno-gpu-curve next to juno-fan-curve; the plain millidegrees
    source /usr/bin/juno-gpu-temp covers native configs).
  * A runtime-suspended dGPU is treated as 25 C rather than queried: reading it
    would wake the card, and the fan belongs at the floor of its curve then.
    An awake card whose nvidia-smi fails falls back to coretemp — a
    permanently failing FCTEMPS source would abort fancontrol into restorefans
    every INTERVAL, which is strictly worse than following the neighbouring
    heat source.
  * fan-profile regen carries and caps both knob lines, and refuses to touch a
    dual config whose GPU helper vanished. The root helper refuses knob mode
    without --gpu-knobs on a dGPU machine, where the CPU curve would otherwise
    drive pwm2 off the wrong temperature. Legacy single-line `# Knobs:` configs
    read back as the CPU fan's curve and are normalized on the next regen.

 -- Marco Barbone <mbarbone@flatironinstitute.org>  Tue, 01 Sep 2026 08:40:00 -0400

juno-kde-fancontrol (0.3.0+diamon1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Multi-point fan curves ("knobs"): click the plot in the editor to add a
    control point, drag any knob, right-click to remove one, up to 16.
  * New /usr/bin/juno-fan-curve, the executable FCTEMPS source behind them.
    fancontrol interpolates one linear segment only, so the knob curve lives in
    a `# Knobs:` comment, the MIN/MAX keys become a fixed transfer calibration
    and juno-fan-curve reports the commanded PWM as a virtual temperature that
    the calibrated segment maps back to itself exactly. A non-zero exit from
    the helper still lands in fancontrol's restorefans path, so a failure hands
    the fans to the EC rather than to a wrong curve.
  * fan-profile: regen carries a knob curve through a hwmon index change
    untouched, status prints the knobs instead of the calibration, and the
    calibrated noise cap is applied to the knobs rather than to MAXPWM, where
    it would have rescaled every commanded PWM by cap/255.
  * juno-fancontrol-apply --knobs re-validates the whole knob list as root and
    refuses --ignore-cap: regen re-applies the cap at every boot, so an
    exemption would hold only until the next reboot.
  * Both DEVNAME entries now come from sysfs in every writer. juno-fancontrol-apply
    and fan-profile hardcoded this board's names, which on any variant reporting
    a different hwmon name would have produced a config fancontrol silently
    rejects on startup.
  * juno-fan-curve reports a missing hwmon as one line instead of a Python
    traceback; the first call after a resume can land before clevofan
    re-registers. The exit stays non-zero, so fancontrol still falls back.
  * A click that lands on a degree a knob already owns now adds the knob at the
    nearest free degree instead of being silently dropped.
  * The editor appears in System Settings, under System beside Power Management,
    as an external module (juno-fancontrol-settings.desktop under
    /usr/share/plasma/systemsettings/externalmodules). Verified against
    systemsettings 6.7.4, which lists it through the same findExternalKCMModules
    path it uses to build its own sidebar.
  * Both GUIs now take every colour from the active KDE colour scheme
    (backend/ktheme.py): the noise cap uses ForegroundNegative, the live marker
    ForegroundPositive, the curve DecorationFocus, guides and hints
    ForegroundInactive, and the tray series the same three accents. Nothing is
    hardcoded any more, and neither GUI forces the Fusion style over Breeze, so
    a scheme switch now moves the charts with the rest of the desktop.
  * Changing the colour scheme while either GUI runs repaints it: the memoized
    scheme read is dropped on Qt's PaletteChange and on a kdeglobals rewrite,
    because the palette event can arrive before the scheme applier has finished
    writing the file. The scheme file is parsed directly rather than through
    QSettings, whose process-wide cache cannot see a same-size rewrite within
    the same second.
  * Secondary text (guides, hints) is held to a 3.0:1 contrast floor against the
    window, so a scheme or a --dark override cannot make it illegible; 3.0 and
    not WCAG's 4.5 for text, because BreezeLight's own ForegroundInactive scores
    3.69 and a higher floor would override the default KDE scheme.
  * Errors on the status line are marked with a symbol as well as the negative
    colour, per the KDE HIG rule that colour must not be the only carrier of
    meaning.
  * Editor affordances: the handle under the pointer grows and takes the hover
    colour, the handle in play shows its own "78 °C -> 47%" readout, and the
    knob count carries the whole curve as a tooltip.
  * The window, the launcher entry and the settings entry share one icon and one
    desktop-file name, so Plasma matches the window to the application on
    Wayland instead of falling back to a generic icon.

 -- Marco Barbone <mbarbone@flatironinstitute.org>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 22:15:00 -0400

juno-kde-fancontrol (0.2.0+diamon1) unstable; urgency=low

  * The package now owns the whole fan stack: fan-profile and fan-calibrate
    move to /usr/bin, the fancontrol drop-in (30-juno-fancontrol.conf) and the
    suspend/resume hook ship with it. No hand-installed /usr/local pieces left.
  * New juno-fan-monitor tray applet: CPU/GPU temperature, fan RPM and PWM,
    network throughput, discrete-GPU power state, total system power, battery
    runtime, and a rolling CPU/iGPU/dGPU utilization chart.
  * fan-profile regen validates every key before rewriting the config; a
    partial /etc/fancontrol is left alone instead of emitting an empty MINSTART
    that fancontrol reads as 0.
  * fan-profile regen no longer assumes two PWM channels; it globs the hwmon.
  * Reject MINSTART < MINSTOP in both the GUI and the root helper: a kick-start
    pulse below the stop threshold cannot restart a stopped fan.
  * Ship the RAPL udev rule under /usr/share (not activated on install).

 -- Marco Barbone <mbarbone@flatironinstitute.org>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:30:00 -0400

juno-kde-fancontrol (0.1.0+diamon1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Initial release: PySide6 fan-curve editor for Juno/Clevo laptops on top of
    fan-profile + fancontrol.service. Draggable curve chart, live sensors,
    presets scraped from fan-profile, pkexec apply with rollback.

